*16 November 2023 – The writ for election is returned; officially declaring all elected members of the 54th Parliament.<ref>{{Cite web |date=16 November 2023 |title=2023 General Election writ returned |url=https://elections.nz/media-and-news/2023/2023-general-election-writ-returned/ |access-date=19 November 2023 |website=Electoral Commission |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250513040608/https://www.elections.nz/media-and-news/2023/2023-general-election-writ-returned/ |archive-date=13 May 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>
*24 November 2023 – A coalition government is formed between [[New Zealand National Party|National]], [[ACT New Zealand|ACT]], and [[New Zealand First|NZ First]].<ref name="1news.co.nz"/>
*27 November 2023 – [[Christopher Luxon]] is sworn in as [[Prime Minister of New Zealand]].<ref name="TVNZ"/>
*5 December 2023 – The Governor-General issued the Commission of Opening of Parliament. The House elects [[Gerry Brownlee]] as [[Speaker of the New Zealand House of Representatives|Speaker]].
*6 December 2023 – State Opening of Parliament
*30 May 2024 – [[2024 New Zealand budget|Budget 2024]] is delivered to Parliament.<ref>{{cite news |title=Budget 2024 at a glance: What you need to know |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/budget-2024/518246/budget-2024-at-a-glance-what-you-need-to-know |access-date=30 May 2024 |work=[[Radio New Zealand]] |date=30 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240530070450/https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/budget-2024/518246/budget-2024-at-a-glance-what-you-need-to-know |archive-date=30 May 2024|url-status=live}}</ref>
