{{Note|One|1}} This change occurred as a result of the elevation of [[Andrew Bayly]], who had previously been elected as a list MP at the 2023 general election, to an electorate seat on 25 November 2023 at the Port Waikato by-election. Bayly resigned his list seat on 13 December 2023, creating a list vacancy.

{{Note|Two|2}} The resignation of Judith Collins took place less than six months before the [[2026 New Zealand general election]] and therefore a by-election to fill the vacancy was not required.<ref>{{Cite web|title=What is a by-election? {{!}} Elections|url=https://elections.nz/elections-in-nz/what-is-a-by-election/|access-date=2020-07-20|website=elections.nz}}</ref>

